    board: tick auger-2026-09-20-23-09-03 — wave closed, two findings filed
    
    Wave of 2 complete (AUG-007 fa6a97b, AUG-006 a2ef761), GITREINS-JUDGE closed as
    the foreman-direct prerequisite (04c6daa), gate green on the merged tree.
    
    Two rows filed from evidence rather than left as prose:
    
      AUG-011  DuckBrain's 429 backpressure. auger's transport now retries it, but
               the test teardown does not — so a 429 during teardown still leaks a
               namespace. And the registry half is not auger's at all: /api/namespaces
               had accumulated 19 rows for directories that were already gone, because
               the registry delete and the directory removal are independent. That is
               a DuckBrain-wide question for every tool that creates a namespace.
    
      AUG-012  This is a PUBLIC repo with NO CI. gh run list is empty and there is no
               .github/workflows at all, so a contributor's PR gets no automated
               verdict while the real gate lives only on this host. Reported as CI
               health this tick: nothing red, because nothing runs.
    
    Both reported honestly rather than papered over. The tick's actual defect (429
    backpressure reaching business logic, plus a leak audit that scanned the whole
    prefix and so failed on a CONCURRENT run of the same suite) is fixed and proven in
    d2dcad3 and 9f6d9c9.
